gradle-wrapper.jar — placeholder
================================

This jar is normally committed alongside `gradlew` so the wrapper
can download the requested gradle distribution. We can't ship the
binary here (no upstream copy is bundled with this repository).

To populate it once:

  # install gradle (any way: brew, sdkman, Android Studio's bundled
  # gradle, etc.). Then in this directory:
  gradle wrapper --gradle-version 8.11.1

That creates `gradle-wrapper.jar` here. After that, `./gradlew` works
without a system gradle — the wrapper self-bootstraps.

If you're using Android Studio, you can also open the `android/`
folder as a project and the IDE will offer to fix the wrapper for
you (File → Sync with File System → "Use Gradle wrapper").
